      "assistant_text": "Perfect! The wiki has a clear answer to your question.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never holding it there in the first place**. Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest agent and Query agent), immediately before those processes start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n\nThis architecture prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential by inspecting environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
